<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Selim II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a>–<a href="/years/1574">1574</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Selim the Blond, Sarı Selim, Selim the Drunkard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Selim II was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from 1566 until his death in 1574, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurrem-sultan">Hürrem Sultan</a>. He secured the succession by defeating his brother Bayezid near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a> in 1559; Bayezid fled to Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and was handed over and executed with his four sons in 1561. Selim did not lead his armies in person, and his grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokollu-mehmed-pasha">Sokollu Mehmed Pasha</a> conducted much of the government. His reign saw the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1570–1571, a heavy naval defeat at Lepanto in 1571, the recovery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1574 and the building of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selimiye-mosque">Selimiye Mosque</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edirne">Edirne</a>. He died after a fall on a marble floor while drunk.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A full Janissary lived in barracks, drew his pay in cash, could not marry until <b>Selim II</b> allowed it in 1566, and in peacetime policed Istanbul and fought its fires; only his own officers could punish him.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ottoman-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Ottoman Empire</a></li></ul></section>
